    <article class="card">
      <h2>Start Here: Your Web Development Journey</h2>
      <p>Welcome! Developer Xperience is a structured, module-by-module path through
        front-end fundamentals, based on the community-driven
        <a href="https://roadmap.sh/html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">roadmap.sh</a>
        curricula. Pick a track below and work through the modules in order —
        every section links back to the overview so you always know where you are.</p>
      <p>The <strong>HTML track</strong> covers the following ten modules:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="html.html#module1">Module 1: Introduction to HTML</a></li>
        <li><a href="html.html#module2">Module 2: How the Web Works</a></li>
        <li><a href="html.html#module3">Module 3: Your First HTML File</a></li>
        <li><a href="html.html#module4">Module 4: HTML Document Structure</a></li>
        <li><a href="html.html#module5">Module 5: HTML Text Elements</a></li>
        <li><a href="html.html#module6">Module 6: HTML Links</a></li>
        <li><a href="html.html#module7">Module 7: HTML Images and Media</a></li>
        <li><a href="html.html#module8">Module 8: HTML Tables</a></li>
        <li><a href="html.html#module9">Module 9: HTML Forms</a></li>
        <li><a href="html.html#module10">Module 10: HTML5 Semantic Elements</a></li>
      </ul>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h2>CSS Roadmap</h2>
      <p>The <strong>CSS track</strong> takes you from selectors and the box model to Grid,
        Flexbox, and design-system thinking, following the
        <a href="https://roadmap.sh/css" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">roadmap.sh CSS curriculum</a>:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="css.html#module1">Module 1: CSS Fundamentals</a></li>
        <li><a href="css.html#module2">Module 2: CSS Layout</a></li>
        <li><a href="css.html#module3">Module 3: CSS Interactivity</a></li>
        <li><a href="css.html#module4">Module 4: Advanced Layout Techniques</a></li>
        <li><a href="css.html#module5">Module 5: Design Systems</a></li>
        <li><a href="css.html#module6">Module 6: Practical Projects</a></li>
        <li><a href="css.html#module7">Module 7: CSS Architecture</a></li>
        <li><a href="css.html#module8">Module 8: CSS Grid Deep Dive</a></li>
        <li><a href="css.html#module9">Module 9: Flexbox Mastery</a></li>
        <li><a href="css.html#module10">Module 10: Final Projects & Review</a></li>
      </ul>
    </article>
    <article class="card" id="about">
      <h2>About Me</h2>
      <p>Hi, I'm Dev X &mdash; a web developer and educator based in Africa. I built Developer Xperience to share what I've learned about HTML, CSS, JavaScript, accessibility, and building for the web.</p>
    </article>

